{
  "_comment": "Generic, company-agnostic taxonomy for the document-store sources (git_docs, google_drive), read by scripts/doctax.py. Every document gets a category (where its note lives under the docs layer), a doc_type, and optionally an entity (customer/vendor/partner/investor/counterparty) - inferred from PATH SEGMENTS and FILENAME TOKENS only, never from content. Rules are evaluated in order; the first match wins. Per-company overrides use the same shape (rules are PREPENDED so they win; `entities` aliases map a token to a canonical name; an `exclude` rule drops a folder from the brain) and live in the user's data dir, never in this repo.",
